[38;5;231m⏺[39m I've put the layout options in a browser tab, since they're easier to see than describe. It should open on its own; if
  it doesn't, use this link:
  [94m]8;id=1k5x505;http://localhost:54988/?key=6345e0168355cec630311c2feee1f112efcd998523b56191dd3a7669badbca75\http://localhost:54988/?key=6345e0168355cec630311c2feee1f112efcd998523b56191dd3a7669badbca75[39m]8;;\. The browser view uses a
  fair number of tokens, so tell me if you'd rather stay in the terminal.

  [1mOn screen:[0m the same 12 fields split into four groups:
  - [1mProfile:[0m name, email, avatar
  - [1mPreferences:[0m time zone, language, theme
  - [1mNotifications:[0m email, push, weekly digest
  - [1mSecurity:[0m two-factor auth, session timeout, API token

  There are three ways to lay them out:
  - [1mA. Stacked sections:[0m one page with a heading per group. This is the smallest change and nothing is hidden.
  - [1mB. Tabs:[0m one group visible at a time. It's more compact, but hides fields and needs a little JavaScript to switch
    tabs.
  - [1mC. Sidebar plus sections:[0m the sections from A, plus a sidebar of links to each one. It needs a wider page than the
    current 640px.

  I recommend [1mA[0m. With 12 fields, tabs or a sidebar would add more navigation than they save, and A keeps the single Save
  button and the [38;5;153msettings.js[39m submit code exactly as they are.

  Which layout do you want? You can click one in the browser and reply here. Tell me too if the groups themselves look
  wrong.

  The mockup files are saved in a new [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m folder inside the project. The repo has no [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m yet, so that
  folder should be ignored before anything gets committed.

